Vendored airunner_common (issue #2243, Gap 1)
============================================

What
----
`airunner_common/` is a verbatim copy of the pure-Python package from the
published airunner-common 6.1.7 wheel (13 files, no dist-info), shipped
as files into usr/lib/python3/dist-packages by debian/airunner.install.
`airunner-common.LICENSE` is the wheel's GPL-3.0-only license text.

Origin
------
- Distribution: airunner-common 6.1.7 (PyPI)
- Wheel: airunner_common-6.1.7-py3-none-any.whl
- Wheel sha256:
  a7d975b72fb0059b3ec466cc793c894f31eb35dbb4345d7592ddf3f4d1cef970
- Upstream repo: https://github.com/Capsize-Games/airunner-common
- Retrieved: 2026-10-09. Every file was verified byte-identical
  against the wheel's RECORD hashes before committing.

Why vendored
------------
airunner-common~=6.1.7 is a hard services import (235 import sites),
but dh_python3 cannot map it to a distro package, so the .deb neither
shipped it nor depended on it and the installed daemon died with
ModuleNotFoundError. This mirrors the airunner_native stanza in
debian/airunner.install: pybuild cannot build two source trees into
one binary package, so the module ships as files. Nothing queries
airunner-common dist metadata at runtime (get_version() resolves
airunner-services first and falls back to package_metadata.VERSION),
so no dist-info is shipped.

Its own wheel dependencies need no extra handling: facehuggershield
is never imported at runtime (package_metadata.py only names the
requirement string), and python-dotenv is already in this package's
dependency closure (services/setup.py CORE_REQUIREMENTS).

Exit criteria
-------------
Delete this directory and ship a real dependency once either holds:

- Capsize-Games/airunner-common publishes its own Debian binary
  (the fix #2243 prefers), or
- dh_python3 can map airunner-common to a distro package.

Then replace the .install stanza below with that binary in
debian/control Depends.
